{"availability":"available","full":"sadhaka/loom-engine","name":"loom-engine","description":"TypeScript runtime for AI-driven worlds. ECS + Trinity Mainframe kernels + a tamper-evident HMAC-SHA-256 EventChain integrity layer. Deterministic replay. BUSL-1.1, built from scratch for TheWorldTable.ai.","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"TypeScript","stars":6,"forks":1,"created":"2026-05-07T09:06:19Z","updated":"2026-07-27T02:08:07Z","license":null,"branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":["ai-game","deterministic","ecs","event-sourcing","game-engine","hmac","typescript"],"demo":"https://loom-engine.pages.dev/demo/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T08:58:45.914Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T08:58:45.914Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T08:58:45.914Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T08:58:45.914Z","stars":6,"forks":1}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A source-available, deterministic RPG simulation core — one Rust engine, five language surfaces, same seed, same result.","The engine resolves the dice and owns the state; an AI narrates the outcome but can never author it. The same seeded simulation runs in TypeScript (npm), Python (PyPI), Rust (crates.io), WebAssembly, and a C ABI and produces byte-identical output on every surface — the basis for replay, server-authoritative anti-cheat primitives, and honest AI-narrated play.","That exact hash is reproduced by npm, the Python port, the Rust crates, the WASM build, and the C ABI - pinned by a shared golden-vector suite (4,259 tests) and enforced in CI by the cross-language determinism gate (.github/workflows/determinism-gate.yml)."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/sadhaka/loom-engine/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"fdd7b0c68d0927d1460840e6008906cb3cfb4207b74d80ff4bace9bee3f1e22b","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T08:58:46.113Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T08:58:46.113Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A source-a